    "updated_at": "2026-05-05T01:21:59Z",
    "body": "Follow-up from a manual source test: if I clone the missing sibling repos into the relative layout expected by the path dependencies, `u-nesting-d2` can build and test:\n\n```text\n/tmp/beambench-u-nesting-full-*/work/U-Nesting\n/tmp/beambench-u-nesting-full-*/algorithms/u-geometry\n/tmp/beambench-u-nesting-full-*/algorithms/u-metaheur\n/tmp/beambench-u-nesting-full-*/foundation/u-numflow\n```\n\nWith that layout:\n\n```text\ncargo tree -p u-nesting-d2  # passed\ncargo check -p u-nesting-d2 # passed\ncargo test -p u-nesting-d2  # passed: 160 unit, 24 integration, 2 doc tests\n```\n\nSo the blocker is specifically clean dependency usability from crates.io / a fresh single-repo checkout, not that the current source is inherently unbuildable when the unpublished sibling repos are present.\n\nFor downstream users, the cleanest fixes would be either publishing `u-geometry` and updating the manifests to use registry deps, or documenting/submoduling the required multi-repo workspace layout.\n",
